# Local scratch: renders, summaries, and the pointer to your own reference
# diagrams. None of it belongs in the repository.
.analysis/
tests/output/

# Derived from whatever reference diagrams you point the learning skills at.
# The digests are salted with an in-repo constant, so committing them would let
# anyone holding a list of candidate names confirm which appear in your corpus -
# the very thing the check exists to prevent.
tests/sensitive-tokens.*.sha256

# Backups written before an in-place update
*.backup-*.drawio
*.backup-*.excalidraw

node_modules/
*.log
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store

# Third-party product logos are cached locally, not committed: they carry their
# own trademark and licensing terms, and generated diagrams embed the image
# anyway. Force-add a specific one if you decide you want it in the repo.
skills/arkitect-drawio/assets/logos/*
!skills/arkitect-drawio/assets/logos/README.md

# Icons built from third-party logos: same reasoning.
skills/arkitect-excalidraw/assets/icons/*
!skills/arkitect-excalidraw/assets/icons/README.md

# A library downloaded on demand from libraries.excalidraw.com is a cache: it
# belongs to its author and is re-installable from the public catalogue.
skills/arkitect-excalidraw/assets/libraries/*
!skills/arkitect-excalidraw/assets/libraries/README.md

# The bundled set is different - it ships with the plugin as the primary source
# of icons, so a diagram can be drawn offline and the same product always gets
# the same mark. Credits are in bundled/ATTRIBUTION.md.
!skills/arkitect-excalidraw/assets/libraries/bundled/
!skills/arkitect-excalidraw/assets/libraries/bundled/**

# The contact sheets are committed as PNGs, which is what anyone reads. The
# scenes behind them are regenerable and add megabytes.
skills/arkitect-excalidraw/assets/libraries/bundled/sheets/*.excalidraw
skills/arkitect-excalidraw/assets/libraries/bundled/sheets/*.svg
